From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Sun, 04 May 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lib: initcall: sun5i MBUS settle before each post-reloc initcall

U-Boot on sun5i/R8 hangs at different initcalls on different boots:
initr_dm, sunxi_nand_probe, and others. Each stall follows the same
pattern: the previous initcall wrote to AHB-connected hardware (CCU,
PIO, etc.); the first AHB read in the next initcall finds the MBUS
arbiter busy with those pending writes and stalls indefinitely.

Fix: add a sun5i DSB + register-only busy-wait (~6 ms @ 1 GHz) before
each POST-RELOCATION initcall (reloc_ofs != 0). Pre-reloc (SPL)
initcalls include DRAM init and clock setup which are timing-sensitive;
the settle is skipped for those.

The loop uses only IBUS instruction fetches and register ops -- no DBUS
reads -- so it cannot stall even while MBUS has pending writes.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
--- a/lib/initcall.c	2026-05-08 17:31:59.549311499 +0200
+++ b/lib/initcall.c	2026-05-08 17:33:47.238994319 +0200
@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@
 #include <log.h>
 #include <relocate.h>
 #include <asm/global_data.h>
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+#include <asm/system.h>
+#endif
 
 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 
@@ -72,6 +75,17 @@
 			debug("initcall: %p\n", (char *)func - reloc_ofs);
 		}
 
+		if (reloc_ofs) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+			unsigned int _cnt;
+			asm volatile(
+				"mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 4\n"
+				"mov %0, #0x2000000\n"
+				"1: subs %0, %0, #1\n"
+				"   bne 1b\n"
+				: "=r" (_cnt) :: "cc", "memory");
+#endif
+		}
 		ret = type ? event_notify_null(type) : func();
 	}
 
